-- title:
--   Determinant at Frobenius of a weight-two residual representation
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field of characteristic $p$ with $p$ prime, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is: a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V = 2$, a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $\operatorname{End}_k(V)$, together with the requirement that $\bar\rho.\rho$ factors through a finite level, i.e. there is an intermediate field $L$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ with $L/\mathbb{Q}$ finite such that $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma) = 1$ for every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, $N$ a nonzero natural, and $\theta$ a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the weight-two Hecke algebra of level $N$ away from $S$, namely the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$. Assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $\ell$ (meaning $\ell$ is a nonunit of $P$) and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (that is, $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acts on the residue field of $P$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$), the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Then for every prime $r \neq p$ — with no restriction relating $r$ to $N$ or $S$ — every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $r$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$, one has $\det(\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)) = r$ in $k$.
--
--   This is the statement that the determinant of a weight-two residual eigen-representation is the mod-$p$ cyclotomic character, evaluated at Frobenius elements: the identity $\det\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r) = r$ is extended from the primes where the Hecke relation is assumed to all primes $r \neq p$. It is used in the study of ramification of the residual representation attached to a homomorphism from the Hecke algebra, in the form cited by [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.isUnramifiedAt_of_not_dvd_sub_one_of_trace_frobenius_sq_ne`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.isUnramifiedAt_of_not_dvd_sub_one_of_trace_frobenius_sq_ne).
